A compact transcript-based comparison may be written as $\begin{aligned}
\mathcal{B}_{\mathrm{tools}} &= \{\mathrm{fists}\},\\
\mathcal{M}_{\mathrm{tools}} &= \{\mathrm{fists},\mathrm{elbows},\mathrm{knees},\mathrm{kicks},\mathrm{close\ control}\}.\end{aligned}$ Within the lecture’s restricted comparison we therefore have $\mathcal{B}_{\mathrm{tools}} \subsetneq \mathcal{M}_{\mathrm{tools}}.$

