The lecture now tests the partition on a small everyday case. Let $e$ denote the event of being cut off in traffic, and let $r$ denote our response. The first classification is immediate: $\begin{aligned}
e &\in \mathcal{X}_{\mathrm{external}},\\
r &\in \mathcal{K}.\end{aligned}$ From here the logic branches.

